    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/harness-projections.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Harness projections: CI writes them, the owner consents to every hand edit",
      "prov:value": "**Owner, 2026-10-09:** generated `.claude/` projections of the knowledge graph\nare written by CI, never by an agent. A workflow step regenerates them and\ncommits them to the PR branch. A hand-edited `.claude/` file needs the owner's\nexplicit consent for each change: the agent shows the exact diff and the\nreason, asks first, and records the consent.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/harness-projections.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Harness projections: CI writes them, the owner consents to every hand edit",
      "prov:value": "**`.claude/` is today's instance of a general rule.** Every coding-agent Tool\nhas config files, and some of them are projections of the graph. The rule is\nthe same for each: CI writes the projections, and a person consents to each\nhand edit. `.claude/` is named here because it is the only agent-host directory\nthe generators write today. Which files a Tool reads, and which of them are\ngenerated, belongs to that Tool's adapter. Securing what the agent may do at\nall is [`agent-permissions`](agent-permissions.md)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/harness-projections.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two kinds of file, two writers",
      "prov:value": "**Why CI and not the agent.** A projection is correct only if it was generated\nfrom the tree that lands. An agent's local run reflects the tree it had, which\ncan be stale by the time of the merge, and a hand-merged projection is how\n`.claude/commands/` drifted both ways before `skill:commands` existed. The CI\nstep runs on the PR head, so the projection on the branch is the one the merge\nwill carry. It is also one writer instead of every session that touched a\nskill."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/harness-projections.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Hand-edited files: consent per change",
      "prov:value": "**A standing waiver does not reach this.** The owner asked for consent per\nchange, so there is no gate class for it in\n[`confirmation-waiver`](confirmation-waiver.md)'s table, and a waiver that\nclaims one is not a waiver. A broad instruction such as \"fix the hooks\" or \"make\nthe session start work\" authorises the investigation. It does not authorise the\nedit. Bring the diff back.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
